course: dictionary
lesson: 15299
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one is right. The word skipper can mean a boat captain, a team captain, a friendly name for a boss, or a small butterfly. «The skipper steered the little boat into the harbour.» Boats have captains, so here skipper means the captain of a boat.
explain: Look for clue words. «Our skipper made the whole team cheer before the match.» Teams and matches tell you that skipper means the captain of a sports team. When you read a word with more than one meaning, ask: what is the topic? Sea, sport, nature or friendly talk?
explain: Sometimes the word is a verb, an action. «She skippered her team to a win» means she was the captain and led the team. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it: if «led the team» fits, you have found it.
fact: Skipper is a noun and a verb: a skipper is a captain, and to skipper means to captain.
fact: A skipper is the captain of a ship or boat, especially a small one.
fact: In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, skipper can also mean the captain of a sports team.
fact: Skipper is also a friendly name for a boss or leader, as in «Okay, skipper.»
fact: A skipper is also a small butterfly that darts quickly from flower to flower. A person who skips, jumping over a rope, is also a skipper.
exercise: «The skipper steered the little boat into the harbour.» What does skipper mean here? | A friendly name for a teacher | A small brown butterfly | *The captain of a boat | A person who jumps over a rope
exercise: Which clue shows that «skipper» means a sports captain in «Our skipper made the whole team cheer before the match»? | The little boat | *The team and the match | The bright flower | The skipping rope
exercise: «She skippered her team to a win.» What does skippered mean here? | Flew from flower to flower | Jumped over the rope | *Led the team as its captain | Sat quietly on the bench
test: «Okay, skipper, I'll sort it out.» Who is the skipper in this friendly talk? | A small boat | *A boss or leader | A butterfly | A sports pitch
test: «A skipper darted from flower to flower in the garden.» What is the skipper in this sentence? | *A small butterfly | A captain on a ship | A person who skips | A team captain
exam: Which sentence uses skipper to mean a person who skips? | *«Ella was a fast skipper and jumped one hundred times.» | «The skipper steered the boat.» | «Okay, skipper, let's go.» | «The skipper scored the winning goal.»
